usb: gadget: atmel_usba_udc: detach before enabling

When U-Boot is started from the SAM-BA ROM monitor, the UDPHS pull-up is
still attached with the ROM's device enumerated. Enabling the controller
without detaching never causes a bus disconnect, so the host doesn't
re-enumerate. Drop the pull-up for 200 ms first.

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/atmel_usba_udc.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/atmel_usba_udc.c
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/atmel_usba_udc.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/atmel_usba_udc.c
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #include <dm/device_compat.h>
 #include <dm/devres.h>
 #include <linux/bitops.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/errno.h>
 #include <linux/list.h>
 #include <linux/usb/ch9.h>
@@ -1175,6 +1176,14 @@
 
 	udc->vbus_prev = 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * Detach first and give the host time to notice. When U-Boot is
+	 * started from the SAM-BA ROM monitor the pull-up is still attached
+	 * to the ROM's USB device, and the host would never re-enumerate.
+	 */
+	usba_writel(udc, CTRL, USBA_DISABLE_MASK);
+	mdelay(200);
+
 	/* If Vbus is present, enable the controller and wait for reset */
 	if (vbus_is_present(udc) && udc->vbus_prev == 0) {
 		usba_writel(udc, CTRL, USBA_ENABLE_MASK);
